    },
    "atom::28ae9179302c3f88f8763f49": {
      "atom_id": "atom::28ae9179302c3f88f8763f49",
      "source_handle": "P0024",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "problem_or_question"
      ],
      "value": "核心问题是：肠道微生物组的失调是否与HIV疾病进程有因果联系，还是仅仅反映了宿主免疫和代谢系统受疾病影响后的继发改变？同时探究ART治疗对这种失调及代谢通路的影响。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c34b473f98dc1a3df1e0ea42dcf2307693386d718055834549140219a91a2d79",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "problem_or_question"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::7fb286b255a943d46830ebcf7ead2e7873913ded0209b64efd9a401276e0c189",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::9ca0638881caa3424c4c5fb2": {
      "atom_id": "atom::9ca0638881caa3424c4c5fb2",
      "source_handle": "P0024",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "research_scope"
      ],
      "value": "研究对象为HIV感染者（PL-HIV）与健康对照者；研究情境涵盖ART治疗前、治疗后6个月及12个月的时间点；范围聚焦于肠道微生物群落的组成变化及其衍生的代谢通路动态。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c34b473f98dc1a3df1e0ea42dcf2307693386d718055834549140219a91a2d79",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "research_scope"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::a27ca7ebcef1161b7a26fa4154f738af21b8e5ca0c22dea9d6458f3f1765e702",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::1beed5cbe59f1132e3562305": {
      "atom_id": "atom::1beed5cbe59f1132e3562305",
      "source_handle": "P0024",
      "field_path": [
        "study_summary_A",
        "work_summary"
      ],
      "value": "本研究旨在探讨肠道微生物组在HIV感染及抗逆转录病毒治疗（ART）过程中的作用，特别是区分微生物失调是疾病的原因还是结果。通过全基因组测序和生物信息学分析，比较了HIV阴性人群与接受ART治疗的HIV感染者在治疗前、后6个月及12个月的肠道微生物组成和代谢通路。研究发现，HIV感染者存在显著的微生物失调，表现为促炎微生物富集和特定菌门比例改变。ART治疗虽能部分改善这种失调，但无法完全恢复，且持续影响某些关键代谢通路（如丙酮酸发酵至异丁醇途径），这与Ruminococcus bromii物种的减少相关。",
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c34b473f98dc1a3df1e0ea42dcf2307693386d718055834549140219a91a2d79",
          "field_path": [
            "study_summary_A",
            "work_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::999bcdf86699b915e5dad8ba27c1a6c33b3314753fb573d57bb8096170e70c3e",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::26f6a19146e4cc66a62c2f5d": {
      "atom_id": "atom::26f6a19146e4cc66a62c2f5d",
      "source_handle": "P0024",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "planning_summary"
      ],
      "value": "该论文提供了HIV感染背景下肠道微生物组失调的具体表型特征（如促炎菌富集、特定菌门波动）及其代谢后果（异丁醇通路异常）。虽然研究对象是HIV而非实体瘤，但其揭示的“病原体诱导的代谢通路改变”及“ART治疗无法完全修复的代谢缺陷”机制，可作为理解其他慢性炎症或免疫调节状态下微生物-宿主互作的类比素材，特别是关于微生物代谢产物如何可能间接影响宿主免疫环境的讨论。",
      "role": "planner_interpretation",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c34b473f98dc1a3df1e0ea42dcf2307693386d718055834549140219a91a2d79",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "planning_summary"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::bfc1348d36f6309cd145a88d80c9551db2b418d0826228b510f6997a6bc8e414",
      "multiple_values_in_field": false
    },
    "atom::fa45074ac801c19969563333": {
      "atom_id": "atom::fa45074ac801c19969563333",
      "source_handle": "P0024",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "不能直接回答ICI在实体瘤中的疗效问题。HIV与实体瘤的免疫微环境差异巨大，此处的微生物变化不直接等同于ICI响应相关的微生物标志物。",
        "contribution": "提供了慢性病毒感染（HIV）状态下肠道微生物组失调的典型特征，包括特定的菌群失衡（如拟杆菌门减少、变形菌门变化）和代谢通路的持续性异常。",
        "facet_id": "F1"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c34b473f98dc1a3df1e0ea42dcf2307693386d718055834549140219a91a2d79",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::1b35890d15747ac5582b2878b440a46a2be768768bdc00841ab7efc2599bec5f",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::fe91af9825c72e72df0f1acc": {
      "atom_id": "atom::fe91af9825c72e72df0f1acc",
      "source_handle": "P0024",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions",
        "possible_uses"
      ],
      "value": "可用于综述中描述不同病理状态下（非ICI领域）微生物组失调的共性或特异性模式，作为对比基准或背景知识，帮助界定“健康”与“失调”状态的微生物特征。",
      "role": "planning",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c34b473f98dc1a3df1e0ea42dcf2307693386d718055834549140219a91a2d79",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "0",
            "possible_uses"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::6efa85a026773a73fc95efd17253b545b99254a15f29054b0eb43e2a3db5a9b4",
      "multiple_values_in_field": true
    },
    "atom::b2e7ffae968b86f2dadae989": {
      "atom_id": "atom::b2e7ffae968b86f2dadae989",
      "source_handle": "P0024",
      "field_path": [
        "review_planning_B",
        "facet_contributions"
      ],
      "value": {
        "boundaries": "所给材料未详细阐述该代谢通路具体如何影响免疫系统或肿瘤微环境。不能将此机制直接外推至ICI疗效机制，除非有额外的文献支持HIV模型与ICI模型在该代谢路径上的同源性。",
        "contribution": "揭示了微生物代谢通路（异丁醇途径）与特定菌种（R. bromii）之间的关联，暗示了微生物代谢活动可能是介导宿主生理状态改变的重要机制。",
        "facet_id": "F2"
      },
      "role": "evidence",
      "origins": [
        {
          "record_id": "record::c34b473f98dc1a3df1e0ea42dcf2307693386d718055834549140219a91a2d79",
          "field_path": [
            "review_planning_B",
            "facet_contributions",
            "1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "variant_group": "field::1b35890d15747ac5582b2878b440a46a2be768768bdc00841ab7efc2599bec5f",
